  "authors": [],
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256",
  "body": {
    "givenName": "iFly",
    "image": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "contentUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/026iFly/swada/main/assets/iFly.png",
      "sha256": "bb9ade5d049213bb6a4bd3455a318ba51397baca407f4f1f2a6c7108f72d5067"
    },
    "motivations": "SUCCESSOR KEY ATTESTATION (August 2026) — iFly's DRep key has been rotated. This DRep (drep1dk4vjsku5yzf8xzzx6ysaxk8l2pypjkza8xq86dvcpaccdwje5r) is being retired. The new and current iFly DRep is:\n\n    drep1zj3lfl9vk9qycx7gau9w23v3pyhwy2yfg5ffdje6qemzwkl36au\n\nThis notice is published from the retiring key itself, so the handover can be verified: only the holder of this key could have published it. Please re-delegate your voting power to the new DRep above. Announcements: https://swada.se\n\nATTESTERING AV EFTERTRÄDARNYCKEL (augusti 2026) — iFly:s DRep-nyckel har roterats. Denna DRep (drep1dk4vjsku5yzf8xzzx6ysaxk8l2pypjkza8xq86dvcpaccdwje5r) avregistreras. Den nya och aktuella iFly-DRep:en är nyckeln ovan. Detta meddelande publiceras från den nyckel som avregistreras, så att överlämningen kan verifieras: endast innehavaren av denna nyckel kunde ha publicerat det. Delegera om din röststyrka till den nya DRep:en. Meddelanden: https://swada.se\n\n— — —\n\nCardano's on-chain governance is one of the more serious attempts I've seen to translate decentralization from a slogan into a working institution. Institutions like that only succeed when people with real-world skin in the game show up to maintain them.\n\nMy perspective comes from three disciplines that share one rule: complex systems only work when you trust the data, the procedures, and the people maintaining them. I'm a commercial pilot for ten years (line + instructor) — so I think about safety culture, redundancy, and how unchecked drift becomes a big problem later. I'm co-founder of Intellishares SA, where we tokenize green-energy assets and deploy blockchain in regulated, real-world contexts. And I serve on volunteer boards (AOPA Sweden, Gävle Sjöscouter, Gävlebygdens Flygklubb), where I've learned what consensus-building feels like when there's no fork option.\n\nI want to help Cardano governance succeed — pragmatically, transparently, and with a long horizon.",
    "objectives": "My priorities as a DRep:\n\nReal-world utility first. I vote for proposals that move Cardano toward concrete adoption — tokenized real-world assets, programmable settlement, identity that ordinary people can use, infrastructure for green-energy investment.\n\nValidator decentralization. A healthy long tail of small, independent stake pools (SWADA among them) makes the network resilient. I oppose proposals that incidentally concentrate stake.\n\nSustainability. Cardano's energy footprint is already an advantage; I want governance that compounds that through verifiable climate work.\n\nTransparent reasoning. I'll publish a written rationale alongside every meaningful vote.\n\nCross-disciplinary evaluation. I evaluate proposals through aviation safety thinking, energy-engineering pragmatism, and product sense. One-axis reasoning is how bad decisions get made.",
    "paymentAddress": "addr1q856gtlurau0wnrz8nzap22cww32wa77p5mu3vdpywgcshl64zph7c4yajs044l004zhdmutkdgnutqkj3q79my7y9vs948aw5",
    "qualifications": "Ten years as a commercial pilot (line + flight instructor). Aviation trained me in continuous risk assessment, procedural discipline, and operating where casual decisions have permanent consequences — directly applicable to governance work.\n\nCo-founder of Intellishares SA, a blockchain-based green-energy tokenization project. I've personally designed and installed solar systems, tested inverters and batteries, prototyped circuit boards, and integrated all of it with on-chain settlement.\n\nBoard service in three Swedish organizations: AOPA Sweden, Gävle Sjöscouter (Vice President), Gävlebygdens Flygklubb (Chair). Each has taught me to balance competing interests, build consensus, and be accountable over multi-year horizons.\n\nLanguages: Swedish, English (fluent), Italian (learning). I operate the SWADA Cardano stake pool — my own ADA is pledged into the network whose governance I help shape.",
    "references": [
